From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 19:23:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reliability core: provider failover, render QA gate, scene
 diversity, live stages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Four exceptional-tier upgrades from the open-source study, built native:

1. Provider circuit breaker + image failover (OmniRoute pattern, MIT):
   - lib/providerHealth.ts: in-memory per-provider breaker (3 consecutive
     transient failures open it, exponential cooldown capped at 10 min,
     success closes instantly). Deprioritizes, never blocks: the admin's
     selected provider is always attempted first as the half-open probe.
   - generateImage() now fails over: on a TRANSIENT error (429/5xx/network/
     timeout) up to two other configured providers are tried, healthiest
     first, each with its own default model; reference images only go to
     providers that accept them. Permanent errors never trigger failover.
   - Stock sources: "auto" prefers the source whose breaker is closed, and
     every search records success/failure into the breaker.

2. Post-render QA gate (OpenMontage final-review idea, reimplemented):
   - lib/videoGen/qaGate.ts verifies every video BEFORE upload: ffprobe
     decodability, duration drift >25% vs the pipeline's target, all-sampled-
     frames-black detection (signalstats YAVG), and silent-narration
     detection (volumedetect) for topic videos. A failing render fails the
     job through the existing credit-refund path — tenants are never charged
     for a black, silent, truncated, or unplayable file.

3. Scene diversity + music energy window (OpenMontage ideas, reimplemented):
   - diversifySceneClips(): no two adjacent scenes show the same footage
     when an alternative exists (least-used clip differing from both
     neighbors; deterministic).
   - musicOffset.ts: ebur128 momentary-loudness scan finds where a music
     track actually gets going; slideshow + topic compositions seek past
     long quiet intros (strictly fail-soft to 0 = old behavior).

4. Real progress stages (replaces the fake 15%/60% bar):
   - video_generations.stage column + VideoJob.stage in the contract.
   - The pipeline reports what it is doing ("Writing the script", "Voicing
     the narration", "Finding the right footage", "Composing the video",
     "Running quality checks", ...) and the studio shows the live stage with
     a progress bar mapped to real pipeline position.

Verified: 106 api tests green across videoGen/imageGen/providerHealth/routes
(incl. real-ffmpeg QA-gate and music-energy fixtures), 11 studio page tests,
root typecheck clean, spec lint clean, codegen committed, db push applied.

